  "releaseNotes": "1.0 - Sanity Linq library\n1.1 - BlockContent library\n1.1.1 - Improvements BlockContent\n1.1.2 - Fixed bug where SanityLocale.Get() would not work with strings.\n1.1.4 - Fixed bug that caused a SanityLocale<object> object to get Translations property with null for all values.\n1.1.5 - Fixed bug in update\n1.1.6 - Support for localized arrays\n1.1.8 - Updated documentation\n1.2.0 - Support for nested Includes / projections\n1.2.1 - Extended tests and improved support for fluid/Linq includes\n1.3.0 - Support for field aliases when joining / including\n1.3.7 - Added support for weak references to SanityReference common type\n1.3.9 - Added support for sanity _key field to SanityDocument common type\n1.4.0 - Support for cancellation tokens\n1.4.1 - Bugfix for weak references\n1.4.2 - Support for \"Contains\" queries\n1.4.3 - Support for IHttpClientFactory\n1.4.4 - SanityFile type added\n1.4.5 - Added support for choosing API-version\n1.5.0 - Updated dependencies and support for source link, some serialization fixes\n1.6.0 - Fixed support for queries with parameters against the CDN endpoint\n1.7.0 - Allow for overriding JsonSerializerSettings for serialization and deserialization\n1.7.1 - Fixed using correct serializer settings in client\n1.8.0 - Maintenance release: updated Microsoft.Extensions.Http to a supported version (CVE remediation); fixed malformed line breaks in ToHtml/SanityHtmlBuilder output (now emits <br />) (#75); introduced Sanity-specific exception types (SanityException base with SanitySerializationException, SanityQueryException, SanityBlockContentException; SanityHttpException now derives from SanityException) and switched argument/state guards to standard BCL exceptions (#72). Behavioral change: the concrete exception types thrown on some paths have changed - catch (SanityException) to handle any Sanity-domain failure.\n2.0.0 - BREAKING: replaced Newtonsoft.Json with System.Text.Json (#71). Newtonsoft.Json is no longer a dependency.\n  * JsonSerializerSettings is now JsonSerializerOptions throughout. SanityClient.SerializerSettings/DeserializerSettings and SanityDataContext.SerializerSettings/DeserializerSettings are now SerializerOptions/DeserializerOptions; SanityMutationBuilder.Build and the SanityClient/SanityDataContext/SanityHtmlBuilder constructors take JsonSerializerOptions.\n  * Block content serializers receive System.Text.Json.Nodes.JsonNode instead of JToken. SanityHtmlBuilder.Serializers, AddSerializer, AddHtmlSerializer, SanityHtmlSerializers and SanityTreeBuilder.Build are all affected.\n  * Model classes should use [JsonPropertyName] / [JsonIgnore] from System.Text.Json. Newtonsoft's [JsonProperty] / [JsonIgnore] are still honoured for GROQ query generation, so existing queries keep working; reproducing them during serialization additionally requires the Sanity.Linq.Newtonsoft package.\n  * Install Sanity.Linq.Newtonsoft to keep 1.x serializer settings, custom Newtonsoft converters, Newtonsoft model attributes and JToken block serializers working during migration. See MIGRATION.md.\n  * Fixed: deserializing a dereferenced reference that carries _key or _weak threw an ArgumentException. Sanity emits _key for objects inside arrays, so this affected real documents.\n  * Fixed: a schemaless (JObject-typed) field emitted a second, malformed projection alongside \"{...}\". Free-form fields now project as \"{...}\" only, and JsonObject/JsonNode/JsonElement are recognised as free-form.\n  * Fixed: chained query operators repeated the ordering clause. The expression tree was traversed twice at every level, visiting the innermost call 2^depth times, so .OrderBy(t).Skip(5).Take(10) emitted \"order(t asc, t asc, t asc, t asc)\" and .OrderBy(a).ThenBy(b) emitted \"order(a asc, b asc, a asc)\". Results were already ordered correctly, so this changes the query text rather than what Sanity returns; update any assertions on generated GROQ.\n  * Behavioural change: an explicit attribute name is no longer camel-cased. 1.x applied its naming strategy on top of [JsonProperty(\"MyField\")], yielding \"myField\"; [JsonPropertyName(\"MyField\")] now serializes as \"MyField\". Names already lowercase or prefixed with _ (all Sanity system fields) are unaffected.\n  * GROQ output, mutation payloads and ToHtml output are otherwise unchanged, covered by an offline golden test suite.",
